.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pepe-worker 1  pepe "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pepe\-worker \- Take a share of a `pepe serve`\*(Aqs distributed runs from this machine, under its own guardrails
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe worker\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-join\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Take a share of a `pepe serve`\*(Aqs distributed runs from this machine, under its own guardrails
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-join\fR \fI<URL>\fR
The `pepe serve` to join: http://host:7878
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
What the server calls this worker: the host name by default
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
A file with the token to join with (the server\*(Aqs token file takes it); else $PEPE_TOKEN
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
